# Dockerfile & Images
Docker me application ko container ke andar run karne ke liye hume Docker Image ki zaroorat hoti hai. Ye image ek blueprint ki tarah hoti hai jisme application, dependencies, libraries aur configuration sab kuch hota hai. Docker Image banane ke liye hum Dockerfile ka use karte hain.

# 1. What is Dockerfile?
Dockerfile ek text file hoti hai jisme instructions likhi hoti hain ki Docker Image kaise create karni hai.
> Simple words me:
👉 Dockerfile = Recipe
👉 Docker Image = Prepared Food
👉 Docker Container = Served Food

Jab hum Dockerfile ko build karte hain, tab Docker usse Image banata hai aur Image se Container run hota hai.

> Example Dockerfile
FROM ubuntu
RUN apt update
CMD ["echo","Hello Docker"]
> Is Dockerfile me:
Ubuntu base image use ho rahi hai.
Package update ho raha hai.
Container start hone par "Hello Docker" print hoga.

# 2. Dockerfile Syntax
Dockerfile line-by-line instructions ka collection hota hai.
> General Syntax:
INSTRUCTION argument
> Example:
FROM node:20
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
RUN npm install
CMD ["npm","start"]

Docker upar se niche tak instructions execute karta hai.

# 3. Important Docker Instructions
> FROM
FROM instruction base image specify karti hai.
Har Dockerfile FROM se start hoti hai.

Example:
FROM ubuntu:22.04
Ya
FROM node:20-alpine
> Q: Why is FROM mandatory?
A: It specifies the base image on which the new image will be built.

